1
00:01:51,111 --> 00:01:52,871
Bicycle or something came through here.

2
00:01:55,811 --> 00:01:56,951
That's a letdown.

3
00:01:57,071 --> 00:01:58,971
Just looks like a whole lot of nothing out here.

4
00:02:06,471 --> 00:02:06,991
Hmm?

5
00:02:08,411 --> 00:02:09,371
Raccoon dog.

6
00:02:09,951 --> 00:02:11,551
See the antlers? I'm a reindeer!

7
00:02:11,931 --> 00:02:13,571
I saw you fall! Are you hurt?

8
00:02:14,311 --> 00:02:15,751
Who the heck is that?

9
00:02:16,811 --> 00:02:17,791
What's going on?

10
00:02:18,111 --> 00:02:20,051
Do you mind? I was sleeping.

11
00:02:20,051 --> 00:02:21,431
Did you hit my friend?

12
00:02:21,811 --> 00:02:24,071
Oh, man! That guy is huge!

13
00:02:24,151 --> 00:02:25,771
I thought we were alone on this island.

14
00:02:27,771 --> 00:02:28,291
Huh?

15
00:02:31,951 --> 00:02:33,031
You know him?

16
00:02:35,311 --> 00:02:37,651
Navy Headquarters Admiral Aokiji,

17
00:02:37,911 --> 00:02:40,211
the ferocity of an ultimate powerhouse.

18
00:02:50,051 --> 00:03:04,611
This guy has Robin scared out of her freaking mind!

19
00:03:04,991 --> 00:03:05,631
Why?

20
00:03:05,631 --> 00:03:15,191
He's a Marine.

21
00:03:16,191 --> 00:03:18,811
Navy Headquarters Admiral Aokiji.

22
00:03:19,651 --> 00:03:20,171
Admiral?

23
00:03:21,171 --> 00:03:23,211
Wait, you mean this guy's an admiral?

24
00:03:23,471 --> 00:03:25,311
That's one of the highest ranks there is!

25
00:03:25,311 --> 00:03:32,311
That's right, there are only three officers in the entire navy who currently hold the position of admiral.

26
00:03:34,491 --> 00:03:38,071
Akainu, Aokiji, and Kizaru.

27
00:03:38,071 --> 00:03:43,871
The only one who outbreaks them is Fleet Admiral Sengoku, the navy's top official.

28
00:03:43,871 --> 00:03:49,731
The man you see standing before you is one of the three men known as the world government's ultimate powerhouses.

29
00:03:49,731 --> 00:03:53,151
But why in the heck is someone like this even here?

30
00:03:53,571 --> 00:03:57,451
Shouldn't you be out hunting some big-time pirates with a bazillion berry bounties or something?

31
00:03:58,191 --> 00:03:59,111
Go away!

32
00:03:59,911 --> 00:04:00,171
Huh?

33
00:04:01,931 --> 00:04:03,211
Oh, my, my.

34
00:04:03,871 --> 00:04:04,991
What? What is it?

35
00:04:05,251 --> 00:04:08,491
Another very sexy lady with super big bazongas.

36
00:04:08,691 --> 00:04:09,511
Are you free tonight?

37
00:04:09,771 --> 00:04:12,051
You watch your mouth, you lanky jerk!

38
00:04:12,431 --> 00:04:13,711
Focus! Pay attention!

39
00:04:13,711 --> 00:04:16,931
Whoa, whoa, hold on a second, you guys.

40
00:04:17,091 --> 00:04:18,571
Couldn't you hear what I just said?

41
00:04:18,831 --> 00:04:20,531
I'm just out taking a little stroll.

42
00:04:21,551 --> 00:04:23,471
Don't get so worked up, okay?

43
00:04:23,651 --> 00:04:25,471
I mean, you guys are just...

44
00:04:25,471 --> 00:04:29,011
You're like just whatchamacallits, you know?

45
00:04:29,551 --> 00:04:30,031
What?

46
00:04:31,011 --> 00:04:31,971
What'd he say?

47
00:04:32,151 --> 00:04:32,971
Mmm...

48
00:04:32,971 --> 00:04:35,811
I forgot. Oh, well.

49
00:04:36,091 --> 00:04:38,391
You're not making any sense, you weirdo!

50
00:04:38,511 --> 00:04:39,491
Robin, are you kidding?

51
00:04:39,811 --> 00:04:41,571
You must be mistaking him for someone else.

52
00:04:41,571 --> 00:04:44,811
This doofus wouldn't pass for a regular marine, let alone an admiral.

53
00:04:45,031 --> 00:04:45,911
Hey, come on.

54
00:04:46,111 --> 00:04:49,111
You shouldn't go around judging people based on their appearance.

55
00:04:50,451 --> 00:04:55,251
The motto I've always lived by as a marine is total, slovenly justice.

56
00:04:55,591 --> 00:04:57,111
Then our judgment was right!

57
00:04:57,371 --> 00:04:59,631
Anyway, what I was saying...

58
00:04:59,631 --> 00:05:01,291
Uh, excuse me a moment.

59
00:05:02,471 --> 00:05:05,011
Being on my feet too long makes me tired.

60
00:05:05,231 --> 00:05:08,231
Yeah? Then maybe you shouldn't have been sleeping standing up, you think?

61
00:05:08,231 --> 00:05:14,651
What I was saying is that I have no intention of capturing you or anything like that, so just take it easy.

62
00:05:15,291 --> 00:05:20,931
I'm only here to confirm the whereabouts of Nico Robin, who hadn't been seen since the Alabaster incident.

63
00:05:21,231 --> 00:05:23,391
As we suspected, she's been with you.

64
00:05:23,891 --> 00:05:25,691
That is one tall piece of apathy.

65
00:05:26,071 --> 00:05:28,551
The only thing high-ranking about him is his nerve.

66
00:05:28,771 --> 00:05:31,991
I'll put some sort of report together for headquarters later.

67
00:05:31,991 --> 00:05:38,171
Now that you've added another crew member who's got a price on her head, your overall bounty has gone up.

68
00:05:38,531 --> 00:05:44,491
One hundred million plus sixty million plus seventy-nine million equals...

69
00:05:44,491 --> 00:05:49,211
Ah, screw it. Some big-ass number.

70
00:05:49,291 --> 00:05:50,411
Just do the damn math.

71
00:05:50,411 --> 00:05:53,551
That's it! Come, go!

72
00:05:53,551 --> 00:05:54,451
Hold on, Yiffy!

73
00:05:54,831 --> 00:05:56,211
Stop it! Stop!

74
00:05:57,731 --> 00:05:59,991
What are you guys doing? Let me go!

75
00:06:00,091 --> 00:06:02,031
Why are you trying to start a fight with this guy?

76
00:06:02,151 --> 00:06:04,591
Are you crazy? He's one of the strongest Marines there is!

77
00:06:04,591 --> 00:06:08,471
I'm not just gonna stand around while this jerk tries to take Robin away from us!

78
00:06:08,591 --> 00:06:12,191
Take it easy. I told you I'm not gonna do anything, remember?

79
00:06:12,611 --> 00:06:14,651
Well, I am! I'm kicking your ass!

80
00:06:14,651 --> 00:06:17,451
Stop it! Damn it! Hold on! Just relax!

81
00:06:17,451 --> 00:06:26,131
So you're really a Marine? I wish we'd known that a lot sooner.

82
00:06:26,511 --> 00:06:28,111
Hey, who are all these people?

83
00:06:29,211 --> 00:06:30,651
Whoa, are you guys okay?

84
00:06:30,911 --> 00:06:32,711
I thought this island was uninhabited.

85
00:06:33,051 --> 00:06:37,791
Well, they're probably castaways that washed up on the shore here.

86
00:06:37,791 --> 00:06:43,511
There was a passenger liner that was reported missing about a month ago, last seen somewhere in this area.

87
00:06:43,871 --> 00:06:46,571
I'm guessing it sank, and these are the survivors.

88
00:06:47,451 --> 00:06:52,911
How are they, Chopper?

89
00:06:53,411 --> 00:06:56,691
Some of them are injured, but it doesn't appear to be anything too serious.

90
00:06:56,931 --> 00:06:59,111
I've got some medicine that should fix them right up.

91
00:06:59,291 --> 00:07:03,571
But the more pressing matter is that they haven't had much to eat in days. Their bodies are weak.

92
00:07:03,711 --> 00:07:07,351
Sanji and Usopp went to see if they could find some food. They should be back soon.

93
00:07:07,511 --> 00:07:09,951
Hey! Sorry it took so long!

94
00:07:09,951 --> 00:07:17,411
I can only imagine how hungry you are.

95
00:07:17,411 --> 00:07:21,511
Take it easy. No need to wolf it down. There's plenty more where that came from.

96
00:07:21,511 --> 00:07:23,191
Yeah, no wolf. There's plenty.

97
00:07:23,191 --> 00:07:25,611
Hey! Why are you eating it? Cut it out!

98
00:07:25,611 --> 00:07:30,411
Ugh. Look, this island may be deserted, but you still could have found food on your own, you know.

99
00:07:30,411 --> 00:07:32,371
You're lucky we came along when we did.

100
00:07:32,371 --> 00:07:35,871
Their ship wrecked in the Grand Line. They're lucky to be alive at all.

101
00:07:35,871 --> 00:07:40,171
Not everyone was so fortunate. We were the only ones on the ship who made it to this island.

102
00:07:40,811 --> 00:07:41,951
So what happened?

103
00:07:43,331 --> 00:07:48,971
We were on our way home from a gourmet tour of Poochie, the city renowned for its exquisite food,

104
00:07:49,631 --> 00:07:56,171
when suddenly our ship collided with a giant frog that was doing the front crawl and shattered it to pieces.

105
00:07:56,711 --> 00:07:59,311
A giant frog doing the front crawl? Seriously?

106
00:07:59,311 --> 00:08:02,311
Besides, frogs normally do the breaststroke.

107
00:08:02,311 --> 00:08:04,651
Awesome! We have got to see this frog!

108
00:08:04,651 --> 00:08:05,911
That sounds crazy.

109
00:08:05,911 --> 00:08:06,951
It's the truth!

110
00:08:06,951 --> 00:08:08,651
Yeah, that was Yokozuna.

111
00:08:08,651 --> 00:08:10,651
Huh? Yokozuna?

112
00:08:10,651 --> 00:08:15,151
After what seemed like days of struggling, we were finally able to make it to this island.

113
00:08:15,151 --> 00:08:20,471
It didn't take long to deplete our food supply. After one month, we were on the brink of starvation.

114
00:08:20,471 --> 00:08:26,271
Then we spotted someone approaching the island. We rejoiced until we noticed he was riding a bicycle on the water.

115
00:08:26,271 --> 00:08:29,271
Come on! That's even more far-fetched than the frog!

116
00:08:29,271 --> 00:08:31,271
Ah, that was me, actually.

117
00:08:31,271 --> 00:08:32,271
Huh?

118
00:08:32,271 --> 00:08:35,271
The only boat we spotted after that looked like a pirate ship.

119
00:08:35,271 --> 00:08:36,271
That was us.

120
00:08:36,271 --> 00:08:43,271
Well, that makes you one of those, uh, uh, those, you know...

121
00:08:43,271 --> 00:08:45,271
Spit it out, damn it!

122
00:08:46,271 --> 00:08:49,271
Oh, man, I forgot! Stop screwing us around, Jack!

123
00:08:49,271 --> 00:08:52,271
Calm down, look at you! Get a hold of yourself! Take it easy!

124
00:08:52,271 --> 00:08:53,271
Didn't you hear me?

125
00:08:56,271 --> 00:08:59,271
I told you, I'm just out on a stroll.

126
00:08:59,271 --> 00:09:03,271
A stroll, huh? Then go take your stroll somewhere else! Get out of here!

127
00:09:03,271 --> 00:09:05,271
Why are you so angry at me?

128
00:09:05,271 --> 00:09:07,271
It's like he's trying to pick a fight.

129
00:09:07,271 --> 00:09:15,271
Okay, whatever. I'll leave, but before I do, you guys should gather your stuff and get ready to leave, too.

130
00:09:15,271 --> 00:09:20,271
Fortunately, I know of an inhabited island that's not too far away from this one.

131
00:09:20,271 --> 00:09:23,271
You should go there and ask him to help you out.

132
00:09:24,271 --> 00:09:30,271
Hey, you guys! Don't believe a word he says! Understand me? This jerk's a marine officer!

133
00:09:35,271 --> 00:09:37,271
So what? Is that a problem?

134
00:09:37,271 --> 00:09:47,271
Oh, that's right. I get it. I guess that makes sense. Normally the marines are your friends and the pirates are the bad guys, right?

135
00:09:47,271 --> 00:09:50,271
Stop it! What's so funny?

136
00:09:50,271 --> 00:09:52,271
Him? How is he gonna help anybody?

137
00:09:52,271 --> 00:09:55,271
I don't know. Heck, I don't even think he has a ship.

138
00:09:55,271 --> 00:09:58,271
Other than ours, there isn't another ship around anywhere.

139
00:09:58,271 --> 00:10:02,271
Let's see. There's no ship and nobody here seems to have a log pose either.

140
00:10:02,271 --> 00:10:05,271
How in the world are they supposed to get to that island anyway?

141
00:10:05,271 --> 00:10:06,271
Oh, they'll be fine.

142
00:10:06,271 --> 00:10:09,271
Nothing you say sounds the least bit convincing.

143
00:10:09,271 --> 00:10:11,271
It's true.

144
00:10:13,271 --> 00:10:15,271
He does have the power to help them.

145
00:10:27,271 --> 00:10:28,271
That should do it!

146
00:10:28,271 --> 00:10:32,271
We loaded them up with food and water. It should be enough to last them for quite a while.

147
00:10:32,271 --> 00:10:35,271
Feels good to do a little work from time to time.

148
00:10:35,271 --> 00:10:39,271
Yeah, no doubt about that. Hey, you know something? You're not so bad.

149
00:10:39,271 --> 00:10:41,271
What do you know? They're hitting it off.

150
00:10:41,271 --> 00:10:46,271
Okay, so now what? Are you gonna swim to that island and drag these guys and all their stuff behind you?

151
00:10:46,271 --> 00:10:48,271
Don't be ridiculous.

152
00:10:50,271 --> 00:10:52,271
All right, everybody. Stay back.

153
00:11:05,271 --> 00:11:17,271
What is that thing?

154
00:11:17,271 --> 00:11:21,271
It's some kind of monster! I bet it's the guardian of this part of the sea!

155
00:11:27,271 --> 00:11:30,271
Hey, you! Run for it! Look out!

156
00:11:30,271 --> 00:11:31,271
Get out of there!

157
00:11:31,271 --> 00:11:32,271
Get out of there!

158
00:11:35,271 --> 00:11:36,271
Ice Age!

159
00:11:51,271 --> 00:11:52,271
A devil fruit!

160
00:12:01,271 --> 00:12:05,271
The sea! It's... frozen!

161
00:12:06,271 --> 00:12:09,271
This is the power of a Navy Headquarters Admiral.

162
00:12:16,271 --> 00:12:17,271
Whew...

163
00:12:31,271 --> 00:12:46,271
It'll stay like that for at least a week.

164
00:12:50,271 --> 00:12:53,271
Head out across the sea in that direction. Take your time.

165
00:12:53,271 --> 00:12:57,271
You should reach the island in about four days.

166
00:13:00,271 --> 00:13:04,271
It's gonna be a little on the chilly side, so be sure to bundle up and stay warm.

167
00:13:05,271 --> 00:13:08,271
Is this... a dream?

168
00:13:09,271 --> 00:13:12,271
The sea has become as hard as the ground!

169
00:13:13,271 --> 00:13:17,271
We can finally cross it! Now we'll be able to get off of this island!

170
00:13:17,271 --> 00:13:19,271
Thank you! Thanks so much!

171
00:13:20,271 --> 00:13:21,271
Thank you so much!

172
00:13:21,271 --> 00:13:24,271
It's a miracle! The Marine granted us a miracle!

173
00:13:24,271 --> 00:13:39,271
All right, then. Time for us to get going.

174
00:13:39,271 --> 00:13:42,271
Right. I'm really happy for you guys. Take care!

175
00:13:43,271 --> 00:13:45,271
I guess there are all sorts of different pirates, huh?

176
00:13:46,271 --> 00:13:48,271
How can we ever thank you for everything that you've done for us?

177
00:13:49,271 --> 00:13:53,271
Not only did you treat our sick and injured, but you shared your food and water with us as well.

178
00:13:54,271 --> 00:13:55,271
Aw, don't worry about it!

179
00:13:56,271 --> 00:13:59,271
Good things happen to good people. Just let fate take its course.

180
00:14:00,271 --> 00:14:02,271
Make sure the children don't catch cold. Keep them bundled up tight!

181
00:14:02,271 --> 00:14:06,271
At any rate, these colder temperatures should keep your food fresh longer.

182
00:14:07,271 --> 00:14:08,271
Thank you all very much!

183
00:14:09,271 --> 00:14:10,271
We will never forget your kindness!

184
00:14:11,271 --> 00:14:13,271
Take care, Straw Hat Pirates!

185
00:14:14,271 --> 00:14:15,271
Bye! Take care!

186
00:14:16,271 --> 00:14:20,271
Be careful on your trip! Save journeys! Goodbye!

187
00:14:21,271 --> 00:14:23,271
That felt really good!

188
00:14:24,271 --> 00:14:27,271
It feels like winter just happened!

189
00:14:28,271 --> 00:14:29,271
Check it out! I can skate!

190
00:14:30,271 --> 00:14:31,271
Awesome, Chopper!

191
00:14:31,271 --> 00:14:33,271
Must be that winter island blood!

192
00:14:36,271 --> 00:14:38,271
How about this one?

193
00:14:39,271 --> 00:14:41,271
You guys are trying to do!

194
00:14:42,271 --> 00:14:45,271
Man, it's cold! I'm freezing!

195
00:14:52,271 --> 00:14:53,271
What is it?

196
00:14:54,271 --> 00:14:55,271
How should I put this?

197
00:14:56,271 --> 00:14:58,271
You're the spitting image of your grandfather, Monkey D. Luffy.

198
00:14:58,271 --> 00:15:04,271
Or maybe I should say, you're just as reckless and hard to figure out.

199
00:15:05,271 --> 00:15:07,271
You knew... my grandpa!

200
00:15:08,271 --> 00:15:09,271
Seriously? Luffy's?

201
00:15:10,271 --> 00:15:15,271
Hey, Luffy, what's wrong? You're sweating!

202
00:15:16,271 --> 00:15:18,271
Uh, nothing! Really! I'm fine!

203
00:15:18,271 --> 00:15:24,271
Your grandfather helped me out once, a long time ago. That's why I'm here.

204
00:15:25,271 --> 00:15:28,271
I wanted to see you and Nico Robin together with my own eyes.

205
00:15:28,271 --> 00:15:35,271
On second thought, maybe I should just kill you.

206
00:15:36,271 --> 00:15:43,271
The government still doesn't consider you a threat, but I know enough of your history to see you're a formidable crew.

207
00:15:43,271 --> 00:15:51,271
You may be few in number, but with the shrewd rogues gathered here, this crew will likely be a problem later on.

208
00:15:52,271 --> 00:16:00,271
Considering the circumstances regarding your initial bounty, the numerous daring actions you've taken, and the speed of your overall progress.

209
00:16:00,271 --> 00:16:06,271
I've fought outlaws for most of my life, but thinking about how you'll turn out scares the hell out of me.

210
00:16:07,271 --> 00:16:12,271
Hey, wait! Hold on a second! You said you were here to check things out, not to kill anyone!

211
00:16:13,271 --> 00:16:18,271
One among you I consider the most dangerous. That would be you, Nico Robin.

212
00:16:18,271 --> 00:16:23,271
So despite everything, you are here for Robin! Now I'm really gonna kick your ass!

213
00:16:23,271 --> 00:16:28,271
The size of her bounty isn't merely a reflection of her strength and power. It also represents something else.

214
00:16:28,271 --> 00:16:32,271
That would be the level of threat and danger that she poses to the world government.

215
00:16:33,271 --> 00:16:39,271
That's why a 79 million Barry bounty was placed on her head at the tender young age of eight.

216
00:16:40,271 --> 00:16:43,271
I'm impressed you were able to survive, especially as a child.

217
00:16:43,271 --> 00:16:49,271
You managed to betray, sidestep, and escape from everyone in your past, and then found a new partner to make use of.

218
00:16:50,271 --> 00:16:57,271
You survived in the underworld by being quick to switch sides, and now you've chosen this crew as your next haven.

219
00:16:58,271 --> 00:17:01,271
That's enough, jerk! I'm not just gonna stand here and let you speak to a lady like that!

220
00:17:02,271 --> 00:17:04,271
What kind of ridiculous grudge are you holding against Robin?

221
00:17:05,271 --> 00:17:06,271
Stop it, Sanji!

222
00:17:06,271 --> 00:17:07,271
I don't have anything against her.

223
00:17:07,271 --> 00:17:14,271
The only connection we have between us is that I let her escape from me one time, but that's about it.

224
00:17:14,271 --> 00:17:16,271
It was a long time ago.

225
00:17:16,271 --> 00:17:22,271
You will all learn soon enough that protecting this troublesome woman leads to nothing but regret.

226
00:17:22,271 --> 00:17:24,271
If you need proof, consider this.

227
00:17:24,271 --> 00:17:30,271
Every organization that she's had something to do with in the past has been annihilated.

228
00:17:30,271 --> 00:17:34,271
Not one single solitary member escaped except for her.

229
00:17:35,271 --> 00:17:38,271
Why is that, Nico Robin?

230
00:17:39,271 --> 00:17:41,271
Shut up, you jerk! The past doesn't matter!

231
00:17:41,271 --> 00:17:42,271
That's right!

232
00:17:42,271 --> 00:17:48,271
If it did, we wouldn't have a dangerous former pirate hunter guy or a degenerate conniving ex-thief woman on our crew, would we?

233
00:17:49,271 --> 00:17:50,271
Don't go overboard!

234
00:17:50,271 --> 00:17:52,271
Who we are now is more important than who we were.

235
00:17:52,271 --> 00:17:57,271
That's right! Robin is our friend! Don't you dare say anything bad about her! You hear me?

236
00:17:57,271 --> 00:18:03,271
I see. So these poor fools don't suspect a thing.

237
00:18:03,271 --> 00:18:07,271
Just get to the point! If you want to arrest me, then why not just do it already?

238
00:18:07,271 --> 00:18:09,271
Prince of Lu!

239
00:18:09,271 --> 00:18:11,271
No! Robin!

240
00:18:11,271 --> 00:18:16,271
